{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "cmeps_templates",
  "description": "Expression-template library for the CMEPS atmosphere-ocean bulk flux computation (stage 2 of the EqESM project): the pointwise laws of flux_atmOcn_large in cesm/flux_atmocn/flux_atmocn_Large.F90 (the Large & Pond / Large & Yeager scheme of the CESM mediator, cesm3.0-alphabranch checkout), transcribed exactly for use by the cmeps_aoflux component. The library carries (a) the Goff & Gratch (1946) saturation vapor pressure over water of shr_wv_sat_qsat_liquid (share/src/shr_wv_sat_mod.F90:942-956, the aofluxes_use_shr_wv_sat = .true. branch of flux_atmocn_Large.F90:217-225; tboil = 373.16 K hard-coded as in the Fortran, wv_sat_use_tables = .false. in the traced run so the analytic form is used, not the lookup table), (b) the saturation specific humidity conversion of shr_wv_sat_svp_to_qsat (shr_wv_sat_mod.F90:351-363: qs = epsilo*es/(p - omeps*es) with the p <= es guard that sets qs = 1, epsilo = 18.016/28.966 and omeps = 1 - epsilo), (c) the Large & Yeager (2009) neutral 10-m drag coefficient cdn(U) = 0.0027/min(33,U) + 0.000142 + 0.0000764*min(33,U) - 3.14807e-13*min(33,U)^6 (flux_atmocn_Large.F90:153-154), (d) the Paulson (1970) unstable stability functions psimhu(x) = log((1+x*(2+x))*(1+x^2)/8) - 2*atan(x) + 1.571 and psixhu(x) = 2*log((1+x^2)/2) (F90:163-164), (e) the combined stable/unstable psi_m and psi_h of F90:258-259 (psi = -5*hol*stable + (1-stable)*psi_unstable(xqq)), (f) the Monin-Obukhov stability parameter hol = karman*g*zbot*(tstar/thbot + qstar/(1/zvir + qbot))/ustar^2 of F90:252-253 as the unclamped stability_parameter, with the CESM constants karman = 0.4, g = 9.80616 m/s^2 and zvir = 28.966/18.016 - 1 as named parameters (shr_const_mod.F90:32, 21, 31), and the sign-preserving |hol| <= 10 clamp of F90:254 as the separate stability_parameter_clamp (sign(hol_raw)*min(|hol_raw|,10)) so the raw value is available to the composed iteration, (g) the exchange-coefficient shift from the 10-m neutral reference to the measurement height c/(1 + c/karman*(alz - psi)) (F90:282-284) and its clamped variant with max(c/karman*(alz - psi), -0.5) used for the wind-speed shift of F90:272, both with karman as a named parameter, and (h) the neutral heat coefficient rhn = (1-stable)*0.0327 + stable*0.018 (F90:238); (i) the solar geometry of the ocean-albedo phase (med_phases_ocnalb_run in mediator/med_phases_ocnalb_mod.F90 with the orbit of shr_orb_decl in share/src/shr_orb_mod.F90:736-814): earth_true_longitude/solar_declination/earth_sun_distance_factor (the Berger 1978 mean-longitude series of shr_orb_decl F90:762-797, ve = 80.5 and dayspy = 365 as in the Fortran) and solar_zenith_cosine (shr_orb_cosz F90:110-159, the no-dt_avg branch); (j) the ocean albedo laws of med_phases_ocnalb_run: briegleb_direct_albedo (F90:500-502), taylor_direct_albedo (F90:505, unpinned: the traced run uses the Briegleb scheme), the ocean_albedo_scheme selection and the full ocean_albedo_visible / ocean_albedo_nearinfrared laws of F90:453-518 (the flux_albav and use_min_albedo branches and the dark-side 1.0 are unpinned by the traced run, which is Briegleb day-side with flux_albav = .false., use_min_albedo = .false.); and (k) the merge laws of the ocean exports (med_phases_prep_ocn_mod.F90): scaled_fraction (the ifrac_scaled/ofrac_scaled/ifracr_scaled/ofracr_scaled of F90:800-813 with the exact frac_sum /= 0 guard), fraction_weighted_sum (the med_merge dp = dp + src*weight accumulation of med_merge_mod.F90:405-412 applied with the esmFldsExchange_cesm_mod.F90 weights) and shortwave_band (the c1..c4 band split of F90:830-834; the Fortran literals 0.285/0.215 carry no _r8 suffix and are therefore SINGLE-precision literals promoted to r8 - 0.2849999964237213134765625 and 0.2150000035762786865234375 - pinned by every traced row of the merge dump). All coefficients carry their SI dimensions (the empirical cdn coefficients are declared m/s, s/m, (s/m)^6 so the products close as dimensionless; the Goff-Gratch 100 is declared Pa since the 10^() factor is dimensionless, with the hPa-to-Pa role documented in the description). All templates are match-less and invoked by name via apply_expression_template with bindings; the shared-math dependencies (psi_momentum -> psimhu_unstable, psi_scalar -> psixhu_unstable) are body references checked as an acyclic DAG at import (esm-spec 9.7.3). Reference: stage1/cesm/components/cmeps/cesm/flux_atmocn/flux_atmocn_Large.F90 and stage1/cesm/share/src/shr_wv_sat_mod.F90."
 },
 "expression_templates": {
  "goff_gratch_liquid_svp": {
   "description": "Goff & Gratch (1946) saturation vapor pressure over water (shr_wv_sat_mod.F90:942-956, GoffGratch_svp_liquid): es = 10^(-7.90298*(tboil/t - 1) + 5.02808*log10(tboil/t) - 1.3816e-7*(10^(11.344*(1 - t/tboil)) - 1) + 8.1328e-3*(10^(-3.49149*(tboil/t - 1)) - 1) + log10(1013.246))*100 with tboil = 373.16 K (the boiling point of water at 1 atm that the scheme was designed with, hard-coded in the Fortran). The 10^() factor evaluates in hPa and the trailing *100 converts to Pa; in the unit algebra the 100 is declared [Pa] so the template closes as a pressure (the dimensionless 10^() factor multiplies it). The traced run uses the analytic form (wv_sat_use_tables = .false., esm.F90:541-547), so the lookup-table interpolation of shr_wv_sat_svp_liquid is not exercised.",
   "params": [
    "t"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "*",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "^",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 10.0,
        "units": "1"
       },
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": -7.90298,
            "units": "1"
           },
           {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
               {
                "op": "const",
                "args": [],
                "value": 373.16,
                "units": "K"
               },
               "t"
              ]
             },
             {
              "op": "const",
              "args": [],
              "value": 1.0,
              "units": "1"
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 5.02808,
            "units": "1"
           },
           {
            "op": "log10",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
               {
                "op": "const",
                "args": [],
                "value": 373.16,
                "units": "K"
               },
               "t"
              ]
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": -1.3816e-7,
            "units": "1"
           },
           {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "^",
              "args": [
               {
                "op": "const",
                "args": [],
                "value": 10.0,
                "units": "1"
               },
               {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                 {
                  "op": "const",
                  "args": [],
                  "value": 11.344,
                  "units": "1"
                 },
                 {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                   {
                    "op": "const",
                    "args": [],
                    "value": 1.0,
                    "units": "1"
                   },
                   {
                    "op": "/",
                    "args": [
                     "t",
                     {
                      "op": "const",
                      "args": [],
                      "value": 373.16,
                      "units": "K"
                     }
                    ]
                   }
                  ]
                 }
                ]
               }
              ]
             },
             {
              "op": "const",
              "args": [],
              "value": 1.0,
              "units": "1"
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 8.1328e-3,
            "units": "1"
           },
           {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "^",
              "args": [
               {
                "op": "const",
                "args": [],
                "value": 10.0,
                "units": "1"
               },
               {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                 {
                  "op": "const",
                  "args": [],
                  "value": -3.49149,
                  "units": "1"
                 },
                 {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                   {
                    "op": "/",
                    "args": [
                     {
                      "op": "const",
                      "args": [],
                      "value": 373.16,
                      "units": "K"
                     },
                     "t"
                    ]
                   },
                   {
                    "op": "const",
                    "args": [],
                    "value": 1.0,
                    "units": "1"
                   }
                  ]
                 }
                ]
               }
              ]
             },
             {
              "op": "const",
              "args": [],
              "value": 1.0,
              "units": "1"
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "log10",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 1013.246,
            "units": "1"
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 100.0,
      "units": "Pa"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "svp_to_qsat": {
   "description": "Saturation specific humidity from vapor pressure (shr_wv_sat_mod.F90:351-363, shr_wv_sat_svp_to_qsat): qs = epsilo*es/(p - omeps*es) when p > es, qs = 1 when p <= es (the guard of F90:357-360; the caller then caps es at p, shr_wv_sat_qsat_liquid F90:439-441, applied at the call site in the consuming component). epsilo = 18.016/28.966 and omeps = 1 - epsilo are the molecular-weight ratios of the CESM constants (shr_const_mod.F90:43-44); the ratio es/p is dimensionless so the template closes as kg/kg (= dimensionless in the unit algebra).",
   "params": [
    "es",
    "p"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "<=",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         "p",
         "es"
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 0.0,
        "units": "Pa"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 1.0,
      "units": "1"
     },
     {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 0.6219705862045155,
          "units": "1"
         },
         "es"
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         "p",
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 0.3780294137954845,
            "units": "1"
           },
           "es"
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "neutral_drag_coefficient": {
   "description": "Large & Yeager (2009) neutral 10-m drag coefficient (flux_atmocn_Large.F90:153-154): cdn(U) = 0.0027/min(33,U) + 0.000142 + 0.0000764*min(33,U) - 3.14807e-13*min(33,U)^6, with the wind capped at 33 m/s inside each term (the Fortran's min(33.0000,Umps)). The empirical coefficients are declared with the SI dimensions that make each term dimensionless: 0.0027 [m/s] over a velocity, 0.0000764 [s/m] times a velocity, and 3.14807e-13 [(s/m)^6] times a velocity to the sixth.",
   "params": [
    "u"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "+",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 0.0027,
        "units": "m/s"
       },
       {
        "op": "min",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 33.0,
          "units": "m/s"
         },
         "u"
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 0.000142,
      "units": "1"
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 0.0000764,
        "units": "s/m"
       },
       {
        "op": "min",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 33.0,
          "units": "m/s"
         },
         "u"
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "-",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 3.14807e-13,
          "units": "s^6/m^6"
         },
         {
          "op": "^",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "min",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "const",
              "args": [],
              "value": 33.0,
              "units": "m/s"
             },
             "u"
            ]
           },
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 6.0,
            "units": "1"
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "psimhu_unstable": {
   "description": "Paulson (1970) unstable momentum stability function (flux_atmocn_Large.F90:163): psimhu(x) = log((1 + x*(2 + x))*(1 + x^2)/8) - 2*atan(x) + 1.571, evaluated at x = xqq = sqrt(sqrt(|1 - 16*hol|)) in the iteration. The 1.571 is the Fortran's approximation of pi/2 (not a computed constant), transcribed as written.",
   "params": [
    "x"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "-",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "-",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "log",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "/",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "+",
              "args": [
               {
                "op": "const",
                "args": [],
                "value": 1.0,
                "units": "1"
               },
               {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                 "x",
                 {
                  "op": "+",
                  "args": [
                   {
                    "op": "const",
                    "args": [],
                    "value": 2.0,
                    "units": "1"
                   },
                   "x"
                  ]
                 }
                ]
               }
              ]
             },
             {
              "op": "+",
              "args": [
               {
                "op": "const",
                "args": [],
                "value": 1.0,
                "units": "1"
               },
               {
                "op": "^",
                "args": [
                 "x",
                 {
                  "op": "const",
                  "args": [],
                  "value": 2.0,
                  "units": "1"
                 }
                ]
               }
              ]
             }
            ]
           },
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 8.0,
            "units": "1"
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 2.0,
          "units": "1"
         },
         {
          "op": "atan",
          "args": [
           "x"
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": -1.571,
      "units": "1"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "psixhu_unstable": {
   "description": "Paulson (1970) unstable scalar stability function (flux_atmocn_Large.F90:164): psixhu(x) = 2*log((1 + x^2)/2), evaluated at x = xqq for the heat/water stability function psixh and at x = xqq2 for the 2-m diagnostic psix2.",
   "params": [
    "x"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "*",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 2.0,
      "units": "1"
     },
     {
      "op": "log",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "+",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 1.0,
            "units": "1"
           },
           {
            "op": "^",
            "args": [
             "x",
             {
              "op": "const",
              "args": [],
              "value": 2.0,
              "units": "1"
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 2.0,
          "units": "1"
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "stable_blend": {
   "description": "The stability-flag blend of the CMEPS if/else branches: stable*stable_value + (1 - stable)*unstable_value, i.e. the stable-branch value when stable = 1 and the unstable-branch value when stable = 0 (the arithmetic rendering of the F90:238, 258-259 selections). Shared by psi_momentum, psi_scalar, and neutral_heat_coefficient.",
   "params": [
    "stable",
    "stable_value",
    "unstable_value"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "+",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "stable",
       "stable_value"
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 1.0,
          "units": "1"
         },
         "stable"
        ]
       },
       "unstable_value"
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "psi_momentum": {
   "description": "Momentum stability function at the measurement height (flux_atmocn_Large.F90:258): psimh = stable_blend(stable, -5*hol, psimhu(xqq)) = -5*hol*stable + (1 - stable)*psimhu(xqq). The stable branch (-5*hol, the log-law linear form) and the unstable branch (the Paulson psimhu at xqq = sqrt(sqrt(|1 - 16*hol|))) are selected by the stability factor stable = 0.5 + sign(0.5, hol) (1 stable, 0 unstable) via the shared stable_blend template. Shares psimhu_unstable by reference.",
   "params": [
    "hol",
    "stable",
    "xqq"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "apply_expression_template",
    "args": [],
    "name": "stable_blend",
    "bindings": {
     "stable": "stable",
     "stable_value": {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": -5.0,
        "units": "1"
       },
       "hol"
      ]
     },
     "unstable_value": {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "psimhu_unstable",
      "bindings": {
       "x": "xqq"
      }
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "psi_scalar": {
   "description": "Scalar (heat/water) stability function at the measurement height (flux_atmocn_Large.F90:259): psixh = stable_blend(stable, -5*hol, psixhu(xqq)) = -5*hol*stable + (1 - stable)*psixhu(xqq), the same stable/unstable combination as psi_momentum with the scalar Paulson function. Also applied at the 2-m reference height with (hol2, stable, xqq2) for the diagnostic psix2 of F90:309. Shares psixhu_unstable by reference.",
   "params": [
    "hol",
    "stable",
    "xqq"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "apply_expression_template",
    "args": [],
    "name": "stable_blend",
    "bindings": {
     "stable": "stable",
     "stable_value": {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": -5.0,
        "units": "1"
       },
       "hol"
      ]
     },
     "unstable_value": {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "psixhu_unstable",
      "bindings": {
       "x": "xqq"
      }
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "stability_parameter": {
   "description": "Monin-Obukhov stability parameter at zbot, unclamped (flux_atmocn_Large.F90:252-253): hol_raw = karman*g*zbot*(tstar/thbot + qstar/(1/zvir + qbot))/ustar^2. karman = 0.4 and g = 9.80616 m/s^2 are the CESM constants (shr_const_mod.F90:32, 21), zvir = 28.966/18.016 - 1 (F90:31); all three are named parameters so the consuming component declares the constants once. The ratio tstar/thbot is K/K and qstar/(1/zvir + qbot) is kg/kg over kg/kg, so hol is dimensionless. The |hol| <= 10 sign-preserving clamp of F90:254 is applied separately by stability_parameter_clamp, so the raw value is available to the composed iteration.",
   "params": [
    "ustar",
    "tstar",
    "qstar",
    "thbot",
    "qbot",
    "zbot",
    "karman",
    "g",
    "zvir"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "/",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "karman",
       "g",
       "zbot",
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "/",
          "args": [
           "tstar",
           "thbot"
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "/",
          "args": [
           "qstar",
           {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
               {
                "op": "const",
                "args": [],
                "value": 1.0,
                "units": "1"
               },
               "zvir"
              ]
             },
             "qbot"
            ]
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "^",
      "args": [
       "ustar",
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 2.0,
        "units": "1"
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "stability_parameter_clamp": {
   "description": "Sign-preserving |hol| <= 10 clamp of flux_atmocn_Large.F90:254 (the Fortran hol = sign(min(|hol|,10), hol)): hol = sign(hol_raw)*min(|hol_raw|,10). The esm sign op is unary and returns +-1 (and 0 at hol_raw = 0, where 0*min = 0 anyway), so the two-argument Fortran sign is emulated exactly: on every value, including hol_raw = 0, the clamp coincides bit-identically with the conditional ifelse(hol_raw >= 0, min(|hol_raw|,10), -min(|hol_raw|,10)).",
   "params": [
    "hol_raw"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "*",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "sign",
      "args": [
       "hol_raw"
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "min",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "abs",
        "args": [
         "hol_raw"
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 10.0,
        "units": "1"
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "exchange_coefficient_shift": {
   "description": "Shift of a sqrt exchange coefficient from the 10-m neutral reference to the measurement height and stability (flux_atmocn_Large.F90:282-284): c(zbot) = c_n / (1 + c_n/karman*(alz - psi)), applied to rd (momentum, psi = psimh), rh (heat, psi = psixh) and re (water, psi = psixh) with the neutral values rdn/rhn/ren. alz = ln(zbot/10) and psi are dimensionless and c is a sqrt coefficient, so the template is dimensionless. karman = 0.4 (shr_const_mod.F90:32) is a named parameter so the consuming component declares the constant once.",
   "params": [
    "c",
    "alz",
    "psi",
    "karman"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "/",
    "args": [
     "c",
     {
      "op": "+",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 1.0,
        "units": "1"
       },
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "/",
          "args": [
           "c",
           "karman"
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "-",
          "args": [
           "alz",
           "psi"
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "exchange_coefficient_shift_clamped": {
   "description": "The clamped variant of the coefficient shift used for the 10-m neutral wind reconstruction (flux_atmocn_Large.F90:272): rd = rdn / (1 + max(rdn/karman*(alz - psimh), -0.5)), u10n = vmag*rd/rdn. The max(..., -0.5) clamp of F90:272 (a guard against the denominator collapsing for very unstable conditions) applies to the momentum shift only, and only in this wind-shift step; the unclamped shift of F90:282-284 is exchange_coefficient_shift. karman = 0.4 (shr_const_mod.F90:32) is a named parameter so the consuming component declares the constant once.",
   "params": [
    "c",
    "alz",
    "psi",
    "karman"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "/",
    "args": [
     "c",
     {
      "op": "+",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 1.0,
        "units": "1"
       },
       {
        "op": "max",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
             "c",
             "karman"
            ]
           },
           {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
             "alz",
             "psi"
            ]
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": -0.5,
          "units": "1"
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "neutral_heat_coefficient": {
   "description": "Neutral 10-m sqrt heat exchange coefficient (flux_atmocn_Large.F90:238): rhn = stable_blend(stable, 0.018, 0.0327) = (1 - stable)*0.0327 + stable*0.018, the Large & Pond ratio Ch/CD selected by the stability factor (0.0327 unstable, 0.018 stable; the commented chxcdu/chxcds names of F90:239).",
   "params": [
    "stable"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "apply_expression_template",
    "args": [],
    "name": "stable_blend",
    "bindings": {
     "stable": "stable",
     "stable_value": {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 0.018,
      "units": "1"
     },
     "unstable_value": {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 0.0327,
      "units": "1"
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "frozen_state_select": {
   "description": "Frozen-state selection for the unrolled stability iteration of cmeps_aoflux_step: frozen = frozen_prev when the previous update already converged (conv = 1), else the freshly passed value. The AoFluxStep applies it to its 4 state INPUTS (ustar_prev/tstar_prev/qstar_prev/rdn_prev), not to its outputs: the Fortran do-while of flux_atmocn_Large.F90:242-290 exits at the FIRST update that satisfies |(ustar_k - ustar_{k-1})/ustar_k| <= flux_convergence, leaving the exit-state fields of update k, which are functions of the pre-converged state (the update k-1 outputs) plus the fixed fields. The input state of the first passing update must therefore be pinned and carried unchanged through the remaining updates of the unrolled chain (the iteration states do not repeat after convergence: on the pinned rows ustar_2 differs from ustar_4 at the 1.8e-4 level), so the parent's 6th mount exit can be fed the pinned 4-input state and recompute the 15 exit-state fields bit-identically. Each unrolled update threads the previous frozen state and the previous convergence flag; on every reachable trajectory of this contraction map the flags are prefix-0s-then-1s, so the 5th mount's frozen outputs are the input state of the first-converged update — and in the no-convergence case conv stays 0 throughout, so the fresh 4th-update values are selected, which reproduce the 5th update through the exit mount, exactly what the do-while leaves after its final pass.",
   "params": [
    "value",
    "frozen",
    "conv"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "==",
      "args": [
       "conv",
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 1.0,
        "units": "1"
       }
      ]
     },
     "frozen",
     "value"
    ]
   }
  },
"earth_mean_anomaly": {
   "description": "Earth mean anomaly lmm [rad] of Berger (1978) as implemented in shr_orb_decl (share/src/shr_orb_mod.F90:789-791): lmm = lambm0 + (calday - 80.5)*2*pi/365 - mvelpp, the mean longitude lambm minus the perihelion longitude mvelpp. calday is the calendar day of interest [day] (nextsw_cday, including the fraction), 80.5 [day] is the vernal equinox at calday 80.5 and 365 [day] the days per year (shr_orb_mod.F90:762-763); the 2*pi factor closes as rad per orbit, so the unit algebra of the template is rad = dimensionless*rad.",
   "params": [
    "calday",
    "mvelpp",
    "lambm0"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "-",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "+",
      "args": [
       "lambm0",
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "-",
          "args": [
           "calday",
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 80.5,
            "units": "day"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "/",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 6.283185307179586,
            "units": "rad"
           },
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 365.0,
            "units": "day"
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     "mvelpp"
    ]
   }
  },
"earth_true_longitude_series": {
   "description": "The Berger (1978) equation-of-center series added to the mean longitude (shr_orb_decl, share/src/shr_orb_mod.F90:792-797): lambda = (lmm + mvelpp) + eccen*(2*sin(lmm) + eccen*(1.25*sin(2*lmm) + eccen*((13/12)*sin(3*lmm) - 0.25*sin(lmm)))), with lmm the mean anomaly of earth_mean_anomaly (bound once by earth_true_longitude) and lambm = lmm + mvelpp the mean longitude. eccen is the orbital eccentricity [-].",
   "params": [
    "lmm",
    "mvelpp",
    "eccen"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "+",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "+",
      "args": [
       "lmm",
       "mvelpp"
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "eccen",
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 2.0,
            "units": "1"
           },
           {
            "op": "sin",
            "args": [
             "lmm"
            ]
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           "eccen",
           {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
               {
                "op": "const",
                "args": [],
                "value": 1.25,
                "units": "1"
               },
               {
                "op": "sin",
                "args": [
                 {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                   {
                    "op": "const",
                    "args": [],
                    "value": 2.0,
                    "units": "1"
                   },
                   "lmm"
                  ]
                 }
                ]
               }
              ]
             },
             {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
               "eccen",
               {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                 {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                   {
                    "op": "const",
                    "args": [],
                    "value": 1.0833333333333333,
                    "units": "1"
                   },
                   {
                    "op": "sin",
                    "args": [
                     {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                       {
                        "op": "const",
                        "args": [],
                        "value": 3.0,
                        "units": "1"
                       },
                       "lmm"
                      ]
                     }
                    ]
                   }
                  ]
                 },
                 {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                   {
                    "op": "const",
                    "args": [],
                    "value": 0.25,
                    "units": "1"
                   },
                   {
                    "op": "sin",
                    "args": [
                     "lmm"
                    ]
                   }
                  ]
                 }
                ]
               }
              ]
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
"earth_true_longitude": {
   "description": "Earth true longitude lambda [rad] of Berger (1978) as implemented in shr_orb_decl (share/src/shr_orb_mod.F90:789-797): lambda = lambm + eccen*(2*sin(lmm) + eccen*(1.25*sin(2*lmm) + eccen*((13/12)*sin(3*lmm) - 0.25*sin(lmm)))) with lambm = lambm0 + (calday - 80.5)*2*pi/365 the mean longitude and lmm the mean anomaly of earth_mean_anomaly, bound once and passed to the equation-of-center series of earth_true_longitude_series, called by reference. calday is the calendar day of interest [day] (nextsw_cday, including the fraction), 80.5 [day] is the vernal equinox at calday 80.5 and 365 [day] the days per year (shr_orb_mod.F90:762-763); the 2*pi factor closes as rad per orbit, so the unit algebra of the template is rad = dimensionless*rad.",
   "params": [
    "calday",
    "eccen",
    "mvelpp",
    "lambm0"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "apply_expression_template",
    "args": [],
    "name": "earth_true_longitude_series",
    "bindings": {
     "lmm": {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "earth_mean_anomaly",
      "bindings": {
       "calday": "calday",
       "mvelpp": "mvelpp",
       "lambm0": "lambm0"
      }
     },
     "mvelpp": "mvelpp",
     "eccen": "eccen"
    }
   }
  },
"solar_declination": {
   "description": "Solar declination delta [rad] of shr_orb_decl (share/src/shr_orb_mod.F90:783-787): delta = asin(sin(obliqr)*sin(lambda)) with lambda the Berger (1978) true longitude of earth_true_longitude, called by reference. obliqr is the obliquity [rad] (the med_phases_ocnalb_orbital_update value for the traced configuration, 0.40910112257977893 rad).",
   "params": [
    "calday",
    "eccen",
    "mvelpp",
    "lambm0",
    "obliqr"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "asin",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "sin",
        "args": [
         "obliqr"
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "sin",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "apply_expression_template",
          "args": [],
          "name": "earth_true_longitude",
          "bindings": {
           "calday": "calday",
           "eccen": "eccen",
           "mvelpp": "mvelpp",
           "lambm0": "lambm0"
          }
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
"earth_sun_distance_factor": {
   "description": "Earth-sun distance factor eccf [-] of shr_orb_decl (share/src/shr_orb_mod.F90:775-781): invrho = (1 + eccen*cos(lambda - mvelpp))/(1 - eccen^2), eccf = invrho^2, with lambda the Berger (1978) true longitude of earth_true_longitude, called by reference.",
   "params": [
    "calday",
    "eccen",
    "mvelpp",
    "lambm0"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "^",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 1.0,
          "units": "1"
         },
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           "eccen",
           {
            "op": "cos",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "-",
              "args": [
               {
                "op": "apply_expression_template",
                "args": [],
                "name": "earth_true_longitude",
                "bindings": {
                 "calday": "calday",
                 "eccen": "eccen",
                 "mvelpp": "mvelpp",
                 "lambm0": "lambm0"
                }
               },
               "mvelpp"
              ]
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 1.0,
          "units": "1"
         },
         {
          "op": "^",
          "args": [
           "eccen",
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 2.0,
            "units": "1"
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 2.0,
      "units": "1"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
"solar_zenith_cosine": {
   "description": "Cosine of the solar zenith angle (shr_orb_cosz, share/src/shr_orb_mod.F90:110-159, the no-dt_avg branch used by med_phases_ocnalb_run): cosz = sin(lat)*sin(declin) - cos(lat)*cos(declin)*cos((calday - floor(calday))*2*pi + lon). calday is the calendar day [day] (including the fraction), lat/lon the point latitude/longitude [rad] and declin the solar declination [rad] of solar_declination. The 2*pi factor is declared rad/day so the fraction-of-day (a day quantity) closes the hour angle in rad; lon enters in the same rad units (the Fortran adds the raw radian longitude).",
   "params": [
    "calday",
    "declin",
    "lat",
    "lon"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "-",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "sin",
        "args": [
         "lat"
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "sin",
        "args": [
         "declin"
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "cos",
          "args": [
           "lat"
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "cos",
          "args": [
           "declin"
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "cos",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "+",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "-",
              "args": [
               "calday",
               {
                "op": "floor",
                "args": [
                 "calday"
                ]
               }
              ]
             },
             {
              "op": "const",
              "args": [],
              "value": 6.283185307179586,
              "units": "rad/day"
             }
            ]
           },
           "lon"
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
"briegleb_direct_albedo": {
   "description": "Briegleb et al. (1986) direct visible ocean albedo (med_phases_ocnalb_mod.F90:500-502, ocean_albedo_scheme = 0): anidr = 0.026/(cosz^1.7 + 0.065) + 0.15*(cosz - 0.1)*(cosz - 0.5)*(cosz - 1.0). All coefficients are the _r8 literals of the Fortran.",
   "params": [
    "cosz"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "+",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 0.026,
        "units": "1"
       },
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "^",
          "args": [
           "cosz",
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 1.7,
            "units": "1"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 0.065,
          "units": "1"
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 0.15,
        "units": "1"
       },
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "-",
          "args": [
           "cosz",
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 0.1,
            "units": "1"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
             "cosz",
             {
              "op": "const",
              "args": [],
              "value": 0.5,
              "units": "1"
             }
            ]
           },
           {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
             "cosz",
             {
              "op": "const",
              "args": [],
              "value": 1.0,
              "units": "1"
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
"taylor_direct_albedo": {
   "description": "Taylor et al. (1996) direct visible ocean albedo (med_phases_ocnalb_mod.F90:505, ocean_albedo_scheme = 1): anidr = 0.037/(1.1*cosz^1.4 + 0.15), with the _r8 literals of the Fortran. NOT exercised by the traced run (ocean_albedo_scheme = 0); transcribed for completeness and left unpinned.",
   "params": [
    "cosz"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "/",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 0.037,
      "units": "1"
     },
     {
      "op": "+",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 1.1,
          "units": "1"
         },
         {
          "op": "^",
          "args": [
           "cosz",
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 1.4,
            "units": "1"
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 0.15,
        "units": "1"
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
"ocean_albedo_scheme": {
   "description": "Direct visible ocean albedo scheme selection (med_phases_ocnalb_mod.F90:498-506): ifelse(use_briegleb == 1, briegleb_direct_albedo(cosz), taylor_direct_albedo(cosz)), the two schemes called by reference. use_briegleb is the ocean_albedo_scheme = 0 flag of the traced run (all 288 dumped rows have use_briegleb = 1).",
   "params": [
    "cosz",
    "use_briegleb"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "==",
      "args": [
       "use_briegleb",
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 1.0,
        "units": "1"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "briegleb_direct_albedo",
      "bindings": {
       "cosz": "cosz"
      }
     },
     {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "taylor_direct_albedo",
      "bindings": {
       "cosz": "cosz"
      }
     }
    ]
   }
  },
"ocean_albedo_visible": {
   "description": "Direct visible ocean albedo anidr (med_phases_ocnalb_mod.F90:453-518), the full law: ifelse(flux_albav == 1, albdir, ifelse(cosz > 0, ifelse(use_min_albedo == 1, max(ocean_albedo_scheme(cosz, use_briegleb), min_albedo), ocean_albedo_scheme(cosz, use_briegleb)), 1.0)). The flux_albav = .true. branch (flat albdir) and the use_min_albedo clamp are NOT exercised by the traced run (flux_albav = .false., use_min_albedo = .false., min_albedo = 0 in all 288 dumped rows); the dark-side branch (cosz <= 0) is also unpinned (all 288 rows are day-side); all are transcribed for completeness.",
   "params": [
    "cosz",
    "albdir",
    "min_albedo",
    "use_min_albedo",
    "use_briegleb",
    "flux_albav"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "==",
      "args": [
       "flux_albav",
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 1.0,
        "units": "1"
       }
      ]
     },
     "albdir",
     {
      "op": "ifelse",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": ">",
        "args": [
         "cosz",
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 0.0,
          "units": "1"
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "==",
          "args": [
           "use_min_albedo",
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 1.0,
            "units": "1"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "max",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "ocean_albedo_scheme",
            "bindings": {
             "cosz": "cosz",
             "use_briegleb": "use_briegleb"
            }
           },
           "min_albedo"
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "apply_expression_template",
          "args": [],
          "name": "ocean_albedo_scheme",
          "bindings": {
           "cosz": "cosz",
           "use_briegleb": "use_briegleb"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 1.0,
        "units": "1"
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
"ocean_albedo_nearinfrared": {
   "description": "Diffuse near-infrared ocean albedo anidf (med_phases_ocnalb_mod.F90:453-518): ifelse(flux_albav == 1, albdif, ifelse(cosz > 0, albdif, 1.0)) - the flat albdif on the day side in both schemes (there is no scheme-dependent near-IR law in med_phases_ocnalb), 1.0 on the dark side. The traced run pins the day-side albdif branch (albdif = 0.06); the other branches are unpinned.",
   "params": [
    "cosz",
    "albdif",
    "flux_albav"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "==",
      "args": [
       "flux_albav",
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 1.0,
        "units": "1"
       }
      ]
     },
     "albdif",
     {
      "op": "ifelse",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": ">",
        "args": [
         "cosz",
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 0.0,
          "units": "1"
         }
        ]
       },
       "albdif",
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 1.0,
        "units": "1"
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
"scaled_fraction": {
   "description": "Fraction scaled by its sum (med_phases_prep_ocn_mod.F90:800-813): ifelse((x + y) == 0, x, x/(x + y)) with the EXACT float equality guard of the Fortran (frac_sum /= 0._R8). Used for ifrac_scaled/ofrac_scaled (from ifrac/ofrac) and ifracr_scaled/ofracr_scaled (from ifrad/ofrad) in the prep_ocn custom shortwave computation.",
   "params": [
    "x",
    "y"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "==",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         "x",
         "y"
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 0.0,
        "units": "1"
       }
      ]
     },
     "x",
     {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       "x",
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         "x",
         "y"
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
"fraction_weighted_sum": {
   "description": "Fraction-weighted sum of an ice-covered and an open-ocean value (the med_merge accumulation dp = dp + src*weight of med_merge_mod.F90:405-412 applied to the ocn exports of med_phases_prep_ocn_accum): ice_value*ice_frac + open_value*open_frac, ice term first, matching the source order of esmFldsExchange_cesm_mod.F90. Used where the two sources carry DIFFERENT weights (the Foxx_taux/Foxx_tauy merges weight the ice and aoflux sources by ifrac and ofrac); the merges whose two sources share the same open-ocean weight ofrac (Faxa_rain/Faxa_snow/Foxx_lwnet) use open_ocean_weighted_sum instead.",
   "params": [
    "ice_value",
    "open_value",
    "ice_frac",
    "open_frac"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "+",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "ice_value",
       "ice_frac"
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "open_value",
       "open_frac"
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
"shortwave_band": {
   "description": "Shortwave band split of the net ocean shortwave (med_phases_prep_ocn_mod.F90:830-834, the import_swpen_by_bands = .false. branch of the traced run): Foxx_swnet_vdr/vdf/idr/idf = c*Foxx_swnet with the c1..c4 coefficients bound at the call site. The Fortran literals c1 = 0.285 and c3 = 0.215 carry NO _r8 kind suffix, so they are SINGLE-precision literals promoted to r8: 0.285f = 0.2849999964237213134765625 and 0.215f = 0.2150000035762786865234375 (pinned by the dump: every traced row has vdr/swnet = 0.28499999642372131). The import_swpen_by_bands = .true. per-band branch (F90:824-827) is not exercised by the traced run (the SICE data-ice component does not export Fioi_swpen_vdr/vdf/idr/idf).",
   "params": [
    "swnet",
    "coefficient"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "*",
    "args": [
     "coefficient",
     "swnet"
    ]
   }
  },
"ocean_absorbed_shortwave": {
   "description": "Shortwave absorbed by the open ocean in one band pair (med_phases_prep_ocn_mod.F90:795-796): fswabs = sw_dr*(1 - albedo_dr) + sw_df*(1 - albedo_df), the direct and diffuse downwelling shortwave of one band pair each attenuated by the matching surface albedo of that pair. Shared by the visible band (fswabsv with the all-sky avsdr/avsdf albedos) and the near-infrared band (fswabsi with the anidr/anidf albedos) of the med_phases_prep_ocn_custom computation. The law is the same as the CLM absorbed_shortwave of clm_templates.esm (SurfaceRadiationMod.F90:701-710) with ocean-band names; it is named distinctly because the two template libraries are imported together and the esm-spec deep-equality rule (esm-spec 9.7.4/9.7.5) would reject same-name non-deep-equal definitions.",
   "params": [
    "sw_dr",
    "sw_df",
    "albedo_dr",
    "albedo_df"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "+",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "sw_dr",
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 1.0,
          "units": "1"
         },
         "albedo_dr"
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "sw_df",
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 1.0,
          "units": "1"
         },
         "albedo_df"
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
"open_ocean_weighted_sum": {
   "description": "Sum of two open-ocean source fields each weighted by the open-ocean fraction (the med_merge accumulation dp = dp + src*weight of med_merge_mod.F90:405-412 applied to the ocn exports of med_phases_prep_ocn_accum): (a + b)*ofrac, the two-source merges of esmFldsExchange_cesm_mod.F90 where both sources carry mrg_frac = 'ofrac': Faxa_rain = Faxa_rainc*ofrac + Faxa_rainl*ofrac (L1940-1942), Faxa_snow = Faxa_snowc*ofrac + Faxa_snowl*ofrac (L1949-1951) and Foxx_lwnet = Faox_lwup*ofrac + Faxa_lwdn*ofrac (L1759-1762).",
   "params": [
    "a",
    "b",
    "ofrac"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "*",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "+",
      "args": [
       "a",
       "b"
      ]
     },
     "ofrac"
    ]
   }
  }
 }
}
